  data: {
    LLM: "Remember that the Ace is the most valuable card (1 point) but it is vulnerable to the 2 and 3. Don't play an Ace unless you know the 2 and 3 are gone or your partner sits behind you to protect it.\n\nThe 'Busso': Use the Knock signal only when you command the suit (e.g., you hold 3-2-K). Your partner is obligated (strategically) to return that suit to you.\n\nCounting the 11/3s: There are 10.66 points in the deck. You must count exactly how many 'pieces' (Figures) have been played to know if the remaining cards are worth fighting for.",
    Player: "Remember that the Ace is the most valuable card (1 point) but it is vulnerable to the 2 and 3. Don't play an Ace unless you know the 2 and 3 are gone or your partner sits behind you to protect it.\n\nThe 'Busso': Use the Knock signal only when you command the suit (e.g., you hold 3-2-K). Your partner is obligated (strategically) to return that suit to you.\n\nCounting the 11/3s: There are 10.66 points in the deck. You must count exactly how many 'pieces' (Figures) have been played to know if the remaining cards are worth fighting for.",
